### Top-nav console

A console with its navigation along the top: the first row is a global bar (product switcher, workspace and data region, search, help, notifications, account), the second holds the section tabs and who is online, and the breadcrumb in the page header drills into a project and back out one level at a time. Next to the sidebar workspace it gives all the horizontal space to the content grid, which suits a team console with few sections (five or fewer) and frequent jumps between products and workspaces; a back office with many, deeply nested sections still reads better with a sidebar.

:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="TemplateShellConsoleDemo" code-lang="vue" title="Top-nav console" description="With focus inside, ⌘K opens the command palette; product, workspace, notifications and account are dropdown menus, with a Data region submenu in the workspace menu; a project card opens its detail and the breadcrumb walks back. All figures are sample data."}
